  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Npc191948 is associated with the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, which is a target of multiple compounds, including (1R,3R,4S,7S,9S,11S,13R,14R,15R)-4,11,13,14-tetrahydroxy-7-[(2Z,4R)-4-(hydroxymethyl)hex-2-en-2-yl]-3,9,15-trimethoxy-12,12-dimethyl-6,17-dioxabicyclo[11.3.1]heptadecan-5-one, 24-Methylenecycloartanone, and 6-(2-hydroxypropanoyl)-4a,7-dihydro-1H-pteridine-2,4-dione. All these compounds are linked to CX-1, indicating a potential mechanism by which Npc191948 may interact with CX-1 through the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14. The evidence suggests that Npc191948 could be a drug target that interacts with CX-1 via this subunit, possibly through a common pathway involving proteasome regulation. The scores from the paths are consistent, but the strength of the evidence varies, with the first path having the highest score, suggesting a stronger association. The relationship is supported by multiple independent targets, but the exact mechanism of interaction remains uncertain.",
